From: GameShellNeo contributors
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: mpfs: retain parent resources through child removal

MUSB child teardown can still access its registers and DMA engine. Keep
the parent clock enabled until the child has been unregistered. Release
the distinct generic PHY that probe registered rather than unregistering
the parent device from its own remove callback.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/mpfs.c b/drivers/usb/musb/mpfs.c
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/mpfs.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/mpfs.c
@@ -358,9 +358,9 @@ static void mpfs_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct mpfs_glue *glue = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	clk_disable_unprepare(glue->clk);
 	platform_device_unregister(glue->musb);
-	usb_phy_generic_unregister(pdev);
+	usb_phy_generic_unregister(glue->phy);
+	clk_disable_unprepare(glue->clk);
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_OF
